 ],
 "balloons": [
  {
   "panel": "page-02-panel-01",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "RAMAYYAN"
   ],
   "text": "He came first in thirty-six. Before you washed up on our shore.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji",
    "ramayyan"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-02-panel-01",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "RAMAYYAN"
   ],
   "text": "We were weak, and Chanda Sahib knew it.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji",
    "ramayyan"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-02-panel-02",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "RAMAYYAN"
   ],
   "text": "His cavalry came through Shenkottai pass like water through a cracked dam.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "ramayyan"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-03-panel-01",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "RAMAYYAN (off)"
   ],
   "text": "They burned villages. They took what they wanted.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": []
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-03-panel-01",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "RAMAYYAN (off)"
   ],
   "text": "They sat on the edges of our kingdom and waited for the Maharaja to come with gold.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": []
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-03-panel-02",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "NAGOJI"
   ],
   "text": "And he came?",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji",
    "ramayyan"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-03-panel-02",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "RAMAYYAN"
   ],
   "text": "He had no choice. We paid. Tribute, they called it. Protection money is what it was.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji",
    "ramayyan"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-03-panel-02",
   "balloon": 3,
   "speakers": [
    "RAMAYYAN"
   ],
   "text": "Fifty thousand rupees the first time.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji",
    "ramayyan"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-04-panel-01",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "NAGOJI"
   ],
   "text": "How many times?",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji",
    "ramayyan"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-04-panel-01",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "RAMAYYAN"
   ],
   "text": "Every year since. Sometimes Chanda Sahib himself. Sometimes his generals. Sometimes just the threat of them.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji",
    "ramayyan"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-04-panel-02",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "RAMAYYAN"
   ],
   "text": "The Dutch watched all of it. They saw a king who had to buy his peace from one direction while they circled from another.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji",
    "ramayyan"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-04-panel-03",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "RAMAYYAN"
   ],
   "text": "Every rupee we paid to Chanda Sahib was a rupee we could not spend on powder or walls.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji",
    "ramayyan"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-04-panel-03",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "RAMAYYAN"
   ],
   "text": "But we did build walls. At Aramboli. At the passes.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji",
    "ramayyan"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-04-panel-04",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "RAMAYYAN (off)"
   ],
   "text": "The Maharaja understood that tribute buys time, not safety.",
   "tail": "tail to the panel edge (off-panel speaker)",
   "cast": []
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-04-panel-04",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "NAGOJI (off)"
   ],
   "text": "I have seen them. From a distance.",
   "tail": "tail to the panel edge (off-panel speaker)",
   "cast": []
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-04-panel-04",
   "balloon": 3,
   "speakers": [
    "RAMAYYAN (off)"
   ],
   "text": "You will see them closer.",
   "tail": "tail to the panel edge (off-panel speaker)",
   "cast": []
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-04-panel-05",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "RAMAYYAN"
   ],
   "text": "Walls cost less than tribute, in the long run. And they do not ride home when the rains come.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "ramayyan"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-05-panel-02",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "DHANAJI"
   ],
   "text": "Their horse were better than ours. Faster on open ground. They knew the passes, knew the water holes.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "dhanaji",
    "nagoji",
    "kayal"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-05-panel-02",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "DHANAJI"
   ],
   "text": "We did not fight them in the open. We let the land fight for us.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "dhanaji",
    "nagoji",
    "kayal"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-05-panel-03",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "NAGOJI (off)"
   ],
   "text": "And the Maharaja refused to give it up?",
   "tail": "tail to the panel edge (off-panel speaker)",
   "cast": []
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-05-panel-03",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "RAMAYYAN (off)"
   ],
   "text": "He gave it up, then took it back, then gave it up again.",
   "tail": "tail to the panel edge (off-panel speaker)",
   "cast": []
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-05-panel-03",
   "balloon": 3,
   "speakers": [
    "RAMAYYAN (off)"
   ],
   "text": "Each time, men died. Each time, we paid in gold and blood.",
   "tail": "tail to the panel edge (off-panel speaker)",
   "cast": []
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-07-panel-05",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "RAMAYYAN"
   ],
   "text": "Chanda Sahib has fallen.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "ramayyan",
    "varma"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-08-panel-01",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "VARMA"
   ],
   "text": "Fallen? Dead?",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "ramayyan",
    "varma"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-08-panel-01",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "RAMAYYAN"
   ],
   "text": "Captured. The Marathas took Tiruchirappalli. Raghuji Bhonsle's men have him in chains.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "ramayyan",
    "varma"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-08-panel-03",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "VARMA"
   ],
   "text": "The Peshwa's war has done what our tribute could not.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "varma"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-08-panel-03",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "VARMA"
   ],
   "text": "Chanda Sahib will not ride south this season. Perhaps not ever.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "varma"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-08-panel-04",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "CHIEF"
   ],
   "text": "The Marathas will want payment for their service. They always do.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "varma"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-08-panel-04",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "VARMA"
   ],
   "text": "Let them want. They are far away. The Dutch are close.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "varma"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-08-panel-04",
   "balloon": 3,
   "speakers": [
    "VARMA"
   ],
   "text": "I will worry about debts when the creditors can reach my door.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "varma"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-08-panel-05",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "VARMA"
   ],
   "text": "You knew this was coming, Sawant?",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji",
    "varma"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-09-panel-01",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "NAGOJI"
   ],
   "text": "I knew Raghuji Bhonsle was ambitious and that Chanda Sahib had made enemies.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-09-panel-01",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "NAGOJI"
   ],
   "text": "But I did not know when or how the blow would fall.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-09-panel-01",
   "balloon": 3,
   "speakers": [
    "NAGOJI"
   ],
   "text": "I have been here, Maharaja, not in Pune. My knowledge is old.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-09-panel-02",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "VARMA"
   ],
   "text": "Old knowledge is still knowledge.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "varma"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-09-panel-02",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "VARMA"
   ],
   "text": "What do the Marathas do with a captured Nawab?",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "varma"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-09-panel-03",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "NAGOJI"
   ],
   "text": "They will hold him. He is worth more alive than dead.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-09-panel-03",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "NAGOJI"
   ],
   "text": "The Marathas are patient. They will extract every pagoda they can before they let him go.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-10-panel-01",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "VARMA"
   ],
   "text": "And while they extract?",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji",
    "ramayyan",
    "varma"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-10-panel-01",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "NAGOJI"
   ],
   "text": "While they extract, he cannot ride south.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji",
    "ramayyan",
    "varma"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-10-panel-01",
   "balloon": 3,
   "speakers": [
    "RAMAYYAN"
   ],
   "text": "Then we have a window. The Marathas have given us a gift, whether they meant to or not.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji",
    "ramayyan",
    "varma"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-10-panel-02",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "VARMA"
   ],
   "text": "Enough talk of Arcot. The Dutch are the enemy in front of us.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "varma"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-10-panel-02",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "VARMA"
   ],
   "text": "Let the Marathas deal with the shadow at our back. We have our own war to win.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "varma"
   ]
  }
 ]
}